-- PAPER-LEARN-PROBATION-SETTLE-1 part 2 of 9 (2026-11-05, charter pillar autonomy, program QNFO.OPS; cluster C8-PROJECTS-GOALS of the roadmap and backlog completion sweep).
-- Settles 25 probationary direct paper learnings (ids 4812 to 4870 of the 225 read on 2026-11-04 23:00Z): each row was read in full (claim, lever, application and the model's apply signal) against the live fleet and given one disposition with its reason.
-- PAPER-LEARN-TRIAGE-1 parked them in probation because its catalogue held 6 mechanisms; the apply signal usually meant the model did not know the fleet already does this. Dispositions: already-in-place (mechanism named, existence read today), rejected (category and specific reason, with what would justify re-proposing), routed (to agent_issues 1000459 TRIGGER-FLAP-1 or goal external-impact-per-dollar).
-- Each goal PAPER-LEARN-<id> (DoD: the learning is settled) then completes on its next probe, and roadmap row GL-PAPER-LEARN-<id> verifies in the hourly loop. Revert one row: UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'probation' WHERE id = <id>.
-- APPLY-BY: ci
-- DB: qnfo-audit
-- Rollback: UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = (SELECT b.fleet_status FROM bak_20261105_c8_pl_02 b WHERE b.id = paper_learnings.id), status_note = (SELECT b.status_note FROM bak_20261105_c8_pl_02 b WHERE b.id = paper_learnings.id), updated_at = (SELECT b.updated_at FROM bak_20261105_c8_pl_02 b WHERE b.id = paper_learnings.id) WHERE id IN (SELECT id FROM bak_20261105_c8_pl_02)

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS bak_20261105_c8_pl_02 AS SELECT * FROM paper_learnings WHERE id IN (4812, 4813, 4814, 4815, 4816, 4817, 4818, 4819, 4833, 4843, 4849, 4850, 4856, 4857, 4858, 4859, 4860, 4861, 4862, 4863, 4866, 4867, 4868, 4869, 4870);

UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'rejected', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 rejected (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; conflicts): Conflicts with PRIORITY-QUEUE-1 (owner directive 2026-10-03): v_issue_queue drains by priority (critical, high, medium, low), then oldest first, and a loop never orders by another key. A transitive-blocker key would reorder the owner''s queue and no blocker edges between issues are recorded to rank by.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 4812 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'already-in-place', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 in place (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; invariants): Fleet-wide cross-system invariants already have standing owners and drift triggers: v_issue_accounting checks entered = open + closed + superseded every tick (silent_drops 0, issues_unaccounted 1 read 2026-11-04T23:24Z), the fleet graph publishes drift findings (fleet_graph_findings_warn 79 read 23:32Z), and each failure mode has an fm- detector contract.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 4813 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'already-in-place', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 in place (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; invariants): Cross-store reconciliation metrics with breach triggers exist: v_issue_accounting reconciles the issue stores, the fleet graph compares declared and live bindings, crons and tables, and mirror-guard and version-bump-guard compare repository mirrors; the metrics are issues_unaccounted and fleet_graph_findings_warn.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 4814 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'rejected', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 rejected (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; no-measured-gap): Issues carry no blocker edges, and the code loop batches queued tasks by file (CODE-BATCH-SAMEFILE-1) under work claims, so an acyclicity check has no graph to run on. Re-propose with a measured case of a batch deadlocked on mutually dependent issues.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 4815 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'already-in-place', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 in place (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; claims): Concurrent sessions already claim independent items in parallel and dependent work stays with one holder: the work-claim service refuses a second claim on the same key (acquired false with the holder named) and lists the in-flight tasks; GET /work-locks read 2026-11-04 showed about twenty live claims by different holders at once.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 4816 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'rejected', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 rejected (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; no-measured-gap): Whether a fix cascades into other closes is the paper''s keystone test for its own roadmap. The fleet grades a remedy by its own metric (remedy_efficacy_30d 0.53) and no keystone issue class is defined for a cascade check to demote. Re-propose with a measured class of issue whose closure repeatedly clears others.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 4817 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'already-in-place', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 in place (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; detector): A fix is not complete without an automated detector: ANTIFRAGILE-1 requires a failure_modes row and an fm-<key> detector contract in the pull request that fixes a defect (v_failure_mode_status reads 569 modes), and an issue closes only on close_evidence from a live measurement.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 4818 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'already-in-place', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 in place (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; human): Blockers that need outside action are isolated from the pipeline: an owner-only step becomes a human_actions card with an IDENTITY-BOUND line and a closing probe (v_human_action_gate grades it), and the loops keep draining other work.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 4819 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'rejected', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 rejected (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; no-measured-gap): Doctrine amendments are owner-governed and land by pull request with a version bump; a rule that every amendment states a falsifiable prediction is the paper''s own practice for physics predictions and no amendment is shown to have been made without one that mattered. Re-propose with such a case and its reversal rate.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 4833 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'routed', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 routed (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; goal-cost): Routed to goal external-impact-per-dollar (qnfo-fleet-control, adopted, program QNFO.OPS), the fleet''s standing goal for a unified cost measured per outcome (cost-per-impact refreshed daily); this learning adds merged PR and verified issue as outcome units. Tracked there with a machine check written by the 2026-11-05 roadmap sweep.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 4843 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'already-in-place', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 in place (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; birth,pred): A filed issue already carries a closing probe and a cadence that a loop other than the filing session runs (qnfo-fleet-control remediationContractsTick and scripts/remediation_consumer.py), and a change carries a dated prediction in decision_log.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 4849 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'already-in-place', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 in place (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; trust): Longevity and volume do not widen a loop''s scope: v_trust_ledger computes trust from verified outcomes only (DOCTRINE-1 readings m-t).', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 4850 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'rejected', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 rejected (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; no-measured-gap): No silent truncation by D1 is shown: paper bodies are hashed and versioned (paper_change_ledger keeps the full prior body in paper_change_bodies, PAPER-LEDGER-1) and a writer that cuts a field does so in its own code under that writer''s test. Re-propose with a stored body whose length differs from its source.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 4856 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'already-in-place', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 in place (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; verifylive): A correction issue does not close on a metadata record: an issue closes only with close_evidence from a live measurement of the artifact (CLAUDE.md issues and evidence), and VERIFY-LIVE-1 requires the change to be merged and verified live before a roadmap item is called deployed.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 4857 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'rejected', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 rejected (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; paper-convention): A pre-registered disconfirmation condition and deadline on every claim is this paper''s own practice; CLAIM-INTEGRITY-1 already holds past-tense claims that carry no evidence, and a new required field on every pipeline claim would be a hard gate with no measured defect. Re-propose with the share of published claims that state a prediction and no way to refute it.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 4858 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'rejected', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 rejected (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; paper-convention): A disconfirming-findings registry with a citation mandate is this paper''s convention for its own program; no fleet position paper is shown to have omitted contradicting evidence, and the pipeline review stage and CITE-FULLTEXT-1 already ground each paper on full texts. Re-propose with a published paper whose contradicting source was omitted.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 4859 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'rejected', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 rejected (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; no-measured-gap): The statement that all indexes held zero external papers is a self-identified bias recorded in that paper''s own correction note; no fleet metric shows a research loop acting on an entirely internal evidence base. Re-propose with a measured corpus count by source.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 4860 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'rejected', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 rejected (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; no-measured-gap): CLAIM-INTEGRITY-1 already holds overstated empirical claims in pipeline papers; a model scorer for certainty language against registry confidence would add a layer with no measured miss, against ENSEMBLE-POLICY-1 (layers stay few). Re-propose with published outreach whose certainty exceeded its source.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 4861 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'rejected', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 rejected (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; no-measured-gap): Fleet budget rules are numeric by construction: each cap is a dollar value in fleet_budget and a breach steers to a cheaper model (BUDGET-SOFT-ROUTE-1); the paper''s missing crossing point was in a qualitative physics argument. Re-propose with a budget rule that named no number.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 4862 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'rejected', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 rejected (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; no-measured-gap): The research pipeline already records each review and revise cycle as events, and a new adversarial role with its own reversal metric needs a measured case where a conciliatory pass hid a regression the next pass caught. Re-propose with that case.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 4863 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'already-in-place', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 in place (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; canary): Ensemble agreement is not the only check: fixed-answer canaries exist (qnfo-chat-canary, the CF-MODEL-EVAL-1 battery, research_golden_runs), and ENSEMBLE-POLICY-1 keeps non-model layers (deterministic gate, reader votes, owner verdict).', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 4866 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'already-in-place', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 in place (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; ens): ENSEMBLE-POLICY-1 already composes checks at different independence: a few small judges from disjoint model families plus non-model layers (deterministic gate, reader votes, owner verdict).', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 4867 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'rejected', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 rejected (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; no-measured-gap): Scaling external audits with ledger scope is the paper''s metrology concern at 10,000 units; the fleet widens only loop scopes and only from verified outcomes through the canonical path, and no widening is shown to have outrun its checks. Re-propose with a widened scope that later proved unverified.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 4868 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'rejected', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 rejected (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; analogy-only): Gauge freedom is the quantum-tomography fact that gate sets with identical statistics cannot be told apart; it implicates no fleet mechanism, since issue attribution rests on run records (issue_lifecycle, fleet_runs, decision_log) not on comparing identical outputs.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 4869 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'rejected', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 rejected (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; no-measured-gap): Correlated failures are handled per root cause: failure_modes records root_cause and blast_radius and recurrence detectors fire within the hour, and CLAUDE.md already treats two signals from one producer as one path. Re-propose with a cross-loop failure correlation the existing recurrence detectors missed.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 4870 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
